Bill Gunshannon <bill@triangle.cs.uofs.edu> wrote:
> Has anyone successfully loaded Red hat 7.1 from the boxed set at CETS
> on a 2100??  Jumpstart worked OK and seems to have prepped the disk,
> but everytime I try to boot fromt he install disk the SCSI seems to
> just sit there issuing timeout messages.

I have no idea about RedHat for Alpha. SuSE comes with a program
named "swriteboot". You need this to write the boot loader onto the
first few blocks of the disk. AND you must leave those few blocks
blank when you partition the disk, first hand. I.e., partition c
is the whole disk and starts at 0, but a must start later, or you
will not have space for the boot loader (bootlx in SuSE).

I never found that mentioned explicitly in the manual, and I stumbled
over that one several times when I started with Linux on Alpha. You
keep forgetting it...

HTH

Wolfgang Rupp



