Yann Marigo <yann@yannos.com> wrote:
> Ok... So NetBSD Kernel is compiled in order to work with the seventh
> release of the firmware... My pb is that NetBSD does not provide
> installation iso. They are saying that i must boot with a floppy...
> There is no floppy on my 3000/300X ...

> How do U have install it ?

Temporarily place a SCSI HD on another UNIX system and 'dd' the floppy image
to the HD.  Then place that HD as well as the one you want to install NetBSD
onto, in the 3000/300X.  Boot off the HD with the floppy image, and install.

I've done this a few times with NetBSD and OpenBSD.  It's a lot easier than
trying to deal with floppies, especially if the system doesn't have a floppy
drive (or one that works).

		Zane



