"Rick Henderson" <nospamalphaman@rickhenderson.net> wrote in message
news:zWkf8.22715$0C1.1910073@newsread1.prod.itd.earthlink.net...
> Hi, I have a PWS500au and tried to install Compaq's Jumpstart
> in order to install Redhat 7.1.  It locked up the PWS during the
> install and it has now changed some of the SRM commands so
> that it auto boots to the hd (dkc 0.0.1004.0) and CTRL-C will
> not stop it from booting untill after it has locked up the system.
> I am not able to do anything in the SRM console after this, since
> it displays all the register information and then halts.  Is there anyway
> to set the SRM back to factory defaults?  I tried flashing the firmware,
> but to no affect.  The only way I can get my SRM console back it to
> disconnect the HD. Since I don't have a before copy of " show * " I
> don't know what Jumpstart changed.  Thanks for any help.
>
When you get the system to a >>> prompt (You should be able to use ^c
or ^p but if you can't then take out the HD as you found out), if
you type
show auto*
then you should see a variable something like autoaction, it is
probably set to 'boot' at the moment.
Use
set autoaction halt
to set it to pause at the chevrons.
Then reconnect the hd and reboot.
Look at the values of the 'boot*' variables, things like the bootflags
and the botdefdev variables tend to get changed by OS installs.
Hope this helps
Adam





