I am working on my DEQNA emulation in progress for my emulator.  KA655
firmware want checksum to check station address when I entered 'b xqa0' at 
>>> prompt.  If not match, it will display CTRLERR message.  Does anyone 
know checksum formula for station address?  I found out that each pair of 
bytes are added and shifted left by one on tracings from log file then 
check results aganist last two bytes (after 6-byte Ethernet address).

I have not implemented ethernet calls to Linux operating system yet so 
that I set up a fake ethernet address like 01:02:03:04:05:06 with checksum
0F:16 (got a result from tracings).  That's why my DEQNA emulation is 
half-implemented on my emulator at this time.

Also, according to NetBSD/vax sources, I noticed that DEQNA is similar
like DELQA.  What is difference between DEQNA and DELQA?  To
detect DELQA by write 1 to interrupt vector register to find out.  If 
zero, then it is DEQNA.

