One big difference was a DM-11 would reliably detect a ringtone, and
hold ring asserted. The others would 'yes it is, no it isn't' with
the ring tone...
 
...

> The DHV11 is a dual or quad (don't remember - I could take apart my
> MicroVAX and find out...) Q-bus 8-line mux.  The DHU11 is a

Quad.

> similar hex Unibus 16-line mux, introduced at about the same time,
> in the mid-1980's.  They were similar enough that they could use the
> same drivers, but were totally different from the DH11.

The DHU was done by the systems group, and VAX engineering kept saying
*NO* until they had a design they liked and that had the bits they
wanted. The DHV did not get beaten up on this way, so they diverged.

I did a comms driver for them, and discovered that they are NOT the
same. Not a big deala for terminal type stuff, but it did bite me as I
remember.

Oh, and there was also the DUH-11 from CSS Germany.  

