> Hi Hilger,
> i had this problem before and solved it.
> 
> Holger <germanhd@usa.net> schrieb in im Newsbeitrag:
> 54239d74.0202220730.887c714@posting.google.com...
> > When I boot up I get a number of errors from RDA0, which I expected:
> > READ/WRITE failed with status 0002 on dra0...
> > Hard error error #5 exer_kid ... rda0...
> > And this one which I don't understand:
> > OS-Type:UNIX console CIPCA driver not started.
> This is the controller for an external unit. Nothing to worry about, because
> normally this controller is not installed, but obviously the driver is part
> of the SRM console. This is not an Error, but just info from SRM, that the
> cipca is not there.
>>> O.K. so that is a kind of W2K error message :-)
> > I now try hard to set up the arrays but running SWXCRMGR from
> > diskettes causes the same error msg. and not one try yet changed
> > anything.
> You cannot setup the array like that, because the old configuration is still
> in the onboard memory and thus you get an error and the programm ends. Here
> is how i did it:
> Take all disks out first and run SWXCRMGR with an empty storage cage. The
> programm will run now and tell you there are no disks. Store this
> information in the card's nvram and close down the programm. Power down the
> unit and put the disks back in. Start everything and run SWXCRMGR again. Now
> the programm will start scanning the scsci bus and detects the disks.
> Arrange them as you like and store the configuration into the nvram of the
> card. Initialize all disks and do not forget to also store the configuration
> on diskette. Mark the position of the disks, just in case you want to play
> around.
> With this i managed to get 3 AS2100 running again with random disks coming
> from other systems.
>>>As described above, my solution worked fine. AND AGAIN MANY THANKS
FOR THE QUICK REPLY!!!
