> there forever, thus producing spurious errors when prev_mode is kernel.

Well, manual said that PROBE instructions use previous mode to maxize mode
(least privilege).  Yes, I set temp value to test them on my emulator.
I now uncommented two lines in emulated PROBE instruction.  Yes,
I made some tests to trying find a bug.

If I set transmit delay to 200, I noticed that CHMK #32 transmitted 
a first character to the console terminal and quickly exited with 
result code #8001 before an interrupt occured from TXCS tell TXDB is 
ready to receive another character.  When all terminal stream is 
finished, it tried to return results but it ended up PROBE test failure 
and returned with #040C error code during AST delivered (IPL 2).  PROBE 
tried probe (access test) executive stack with previous mode (supervisor)!
