Hi Susan,

I don't remember whether the on-board controller in the AlphaServer 1000
was a wide or narrow variant, nor whether the the shelf would support
the wide disks (-VW types).

The id's of the lower part of the shelf screwed me for a while in a
1000A - I'd assumed that they ran with 0 at the bottom, 1 next and 2 at
the top - IIRC they ran the opposite way around so having a disk that
defaulted to 0 in the top slot of the lower shelf screwed things up
royally!

I'd try putting just one disk in the part of the shelf you're concerned
with and see what that does for you.  Try a narrow one if you can (like
an RZ28-VA) and perhaps try using the SCSI that the tape and CD are on -
if you can see them then at least you know that one's working.

Good luck.
Steve.


