>>I have used my 3000/300X for some months using a serial console, without a
>>problem. I recently got a monitor for this system, so I devided to hook it up
>>and use the graphics console. 
>>
>>Any ideas? 
> 
> AFAIK, the switch to change the console is _not_ on the MoBo.
> It is on the outside/backside (S3) or it is a SRM command
> (>>>SET CONSOLE GRAPHICS). I don't know the 300X so I can't give
> a definite answer. Someone has to jump in.

  The W1 switch does change the console on the 3000/300X m/b, and pins
1-2 should give you graphics mode.  However, if you don't have a
keyboard and a display connected, the 300x defaults back to a serial
console regardless of the jumper settings.
  I'll look at the SRM settings on my 300x this evening and post
results. FWIW, with the W1 jumper on 1-2 and no keyboard or display, the
DB25 serial port is console.  With kbd/mouse/monitor connected, graphics
console is automagic.  Haven't tried it without the mouse, but i don't
think it matters.  Are you running a turbochannel graphics adapter, or
the onboard graphics?

	Doc


