Hello folks:

Does anyone know what is bug check message #03C0?

With my VAX (TS10) emulator, I finally found a serious bug that cause 
OpenVMS to crash quietly.  That were PROBER/PROBEW instructions.  I fixed 
it and OpenVMS finally displayed date/time dialog prompt.  I did entered 
that.  Then OpenVMS displayed information about devices and asked me to 
answer 'yes'.  I did.  Then finally a dollar.  I entered backup command to
restore system disk.  That was highly successful.

Then I rebooted system.  I encountered another two bugs but fixed them 
quickly.  It cause my VAX emulator system to crash into segmentation 
fault.  GNU debugger immediately showed me that is a bug. :-)  It was FFC 
and EXTZV (bug in operand decoder) instructions.

Then I booted OpenVMS through banner, time/date dialog, and the secondary
installation procedure banner then crashed quietly.  According to my 
debug.log, OpenVMS loaded LOGINOUT, DCL, DCLTABLES into memory then 
executed STARTUP.INS.  Say statement (defined as 'write sys$output')
printed the 'OpenVMS VAX V7.2 Installation Procedure' then crashed
quietly with bug check #3C0 message.  Bugcheck message did not displayed
on my screen but my TS10 emulator recorded BUGW/BUGL instructions with
following message into debug.log file.

Thank you!

-- Tim Stark

