In comp.sys.dec sword7@speakeasy.org wrote:
> Does anyone know what is bug check message #03C0?

Well, I recorded tracings of execution contains BUGW #3C0.  It occurs at
80FB4FF3.  That routine checked 4(AP) for 5AC but its content is
40C.  It resulted BUGW #3C0.

I searched for that cause before BUGW #3C0.  I found that OpenVMS
tried to return results back to DCL interpreter but access violation
was reported by PROBEW.  I noticed that previous mode is supervisor
but it attempted to probe executive stack instead but resulted access
violation.  With result of access violation, put 40C on it.  It happened 
immediately in user-return routine after finished output to the console 
terminal and context switch (LDPCTX) in the same system call (in IPL 2 - 
AST delivered from REI).  It never return back to DCL interprter.

If pervious mode is supervisor, PROBEW instruction tried to probe
area by using executive mode, it resulted access violation and next 
instruction (BEQ) jumped out instead of final return back to DCL 
interpreter.

I believe that DCL interpreter is running in supervisor mode (both
current and previous mode in PSL).  Also, DCL is in system space, 
not process space.

I am searching for the cause elsewhere before PROBE/BUGW problems.  
I have to find the cause to able fix that bugs in my VAX emulator.
I will keep you posted later when something happens.

Does anyone know about that (famailar like that)?

Thank you!

-- Tim Stark

