A RQDX3 can also handle a RD54.  The dead drive he has, is a RD53.  I would
*HIGHLY* recommend moving away from RD53's to either RD54's or else get a
3rd party ESDI or SCSI controller (SCSI controllers typically cost real
money).  

If this is a hobbyist system, the best answer might be to pick up either a
VS3100 or VS4000 off of eBay as they're a LOT smaller, faster, and with a
couple exceptions support SCSI.  I'd personally recommend either a
VAXstation 4000/VLC, 4000/60, or 4000/90. Of course if running VMS is where
your real interests lay, you might want to look at a low-end DEC Alpha.

