In comp.sys.dec sword7@speakeasy.org wrote:
> I am searching for the cause elsewhere before PROBE/BUGW problems.  
> I have to find the cause to able fix that bugs in my VAX emulator.
> I will keep you posted later when something happens.

Good news!  I was able narrowed down to the area that cause bug check 
#3C0 and system-wide crash.  I carefully studied tracings from my 
debug.log and found the problem.  DCL interpreter called system call 
throught CHME #0023 to print something on the console terminal.  Then
it called CHMK #0032 to submit a request to terminal driver to print
something.  After first interrupt from console device to tell that
character was transmitted done, CHMK #0032 prematurely exited out
but terminal stream still was in effect until all characters were
transmitted.  When it was done, it sent software interrupt to IPL 8, then 
4, then final 2.  In IPL 2, it attempted to return results but CHMK #0032
already exited and instead jumped into Bug Check #03C0.

On my VAX emulator (TS10), I tested it by set transmit delay to zero
to block CHMK #32 from prematurely exits and all problems disappeared!
But.... STARTUP.INS now printed information about model, free blocks, cpu 
type, etc.. Then it asked me for date/time 2nd time to enter.  I did that 
and it crashed the same with Bug Check #3C0 (same bug hit)....

I am still working on it to find a bug around first interrupt from
console device for both input and output direction. 

