Hello folks:

Well, I studied entire CHMK #32 tracings but found nothing is wrong
with that.  Bugs had not found yet.  I decided to commented out two
lines in emulated PROBE instruction (check previous mode for requested
mode) and recompiled my TS10 (VAX) emulator to see what happens...

All problems disappeared and OpenVMS get so much (infinitely) further!
I successfully completed the secondary OpenVMS installation.  I rebooted
system and booted OpenVMS through messages from OPCOM, etc into the 
userland and finally 'Username:'!  I was able logged into system with
out any problems.

I tested some commands like 'sh user', 'sh system', etc..  They worked so
well. However, OpenVMS complaint about a few things.  Some logical
names 'no matched' error messages, and a few access violation messages
during STARTUP.COM scripts.  OpenVMS did not tell me a bug check
message but it was found in my debug.log file - Bug Check #474.

I believe that some problems in PROBE instructions or a problem in
terminal stream routines ($QIO - queue I/O system).  Does anyone
have complete information about PROBE instructions with their inner
workings?  My VAX arch manual (1st edition) said that PROBE must
check perivous mode in PSL for requested mode (1st operand).  If
pervious mode is higher than requested mode, changed requested mode
to match previous mode or higher (least privilege).

Thank you!

