Good News!!  Well, I found a serious bug in TS10 emulator that cause the 
OpenVMS stalled after RQDX3 initialization.  I found that by using two 
log files from Simh and TS10 emulators and comparing difference between 
them.  I fixed it in my RQDX3 emulation (rq_PutDesc) to not put 1 on 
command interrupt unless commands slot is only one or previous 
command descriptor belongs to RQDX3 controller.  After it was fixed,
OpenVMS now is trying read blocks from the Installation CD but stalled - 
another bug showed up! :-(

I quickly found another bug when I debugged disassembled traces from
my debug.log.  REMQUE tried to dequeue entry but queue already is empty 
during MSCP read routine.  I searched for cause by using two logs from 
Simh and TS10 emulators and found a cause between sequence initialization 
step 1 and step 2.  On Simh, OpenVMS enqueued read access requests 
by using INSQUE instruction during MSCP initialization step #1 but it 
never happened in my debug.log from TS10 emulator.  There was long 
execution between step #1 and step #2 - estimated 300,000 lines!  I
am narrowing down between step #1 and step #2 to find specific 
area that has a bug.

Yes, after a bug was fixed, OpenVMS got slightly further due to another
bug.  Whew.

That's why debuggers and programmers are blind without their source codes.  
With source codes, bugs can be find much easilier. :-(

