I'm trying to find out whether Tru64 has some equivalent
of Solaris' gethrtime() function.

The gethrtime() fn returns a number of nanosecs relative
to some arbitrary point in the past (not necessarily the
Epoch) and (most importantly for me) is guaranteed to be
always monotonic-increasing. I.e: it never jumps backwards
even if the system time is unexpectedly stepped backwards
