I wouldn't buy one of these, certainly not at dealer prices (I'm
surprised a reputable dealer would sell them).  Unless you replace
a dozen or so ICs on the bottom of the motherboard you'll find that
the machine eventually becomes extremely unreliable.  So if you buy
one, you've got a pretty significant surface-mount job in front of
you; probably cheaper in time-is-money terms to find some other small
box that can do your job.

Intel multias are actually faster for many tasks because of the crippled
memory and I/O on the 21066 anyway; and there are many Intel-multia-like
boxes available at decent prices from other vendors now.

