In article <a3bc69$3kf$1@bob.news.rcn.net>,  <jmfbahciv@aol.com> wrote:
> Portable???!!!  What are you talking about?  The purpose of an OS
> is to deliver computing services to the user.

The purpose of the OS is to manage resources on behalf of application programs.

A portable OS is one that provides the same abstraction on multiple platforms.

The implementation may be slightly or even significantly different, depending
on the hardware design and how the OS is laid out... but there's a clear
advantage to not making people rewrite their apps every time they get a new
computer.

Of course if you're the hardware manufacturer, having the apps be an barrier
to your customers leaving you is a bonus.

